// Knevo patient app — code-signing configuration.
//
// Code signing is PER-DEVELOPER. Each machine sets its own team (and, if
// needed, its own bundle id) in `Signing.local.xcconfig` — that file is
// git-ignored, so developers never overwrite each other's signing setup.
// The local file is optional: without it, the defaults below apply.
//
// Why a developer may need their own bundle id: an explicit App ID is globally
// unique across Apple. `com.knevo.patient` is registered to the owning team, so
// anyone NOT on that team must pick their own (e.g. com.<you>.knevo.patient)
// and use their own personal DEVELOPMENT_TEAM. A free Apple ID works for
// running on your own device (profiles expire after 7 days).
//
// Setup: copy `Signing.local.xcconfig.template` to `Signing.local.xcconfig`
// and fill in your values.

KNEVO_BUNDLE_ID = com.knevo.patient
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// Optional per-developer overrides (git-ignored). Included last so it wins.
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
